From 979415640e625f52956058d76b64dec4cdaab41d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:14:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 38/40] serve: STRATA_SLOT_PARK=1 parks a pipelined slot's
 conversation, reply included

With pipelined slot groups a finished slot is wiped by the next window of
its group that runs it as a pad row, or overwritten by the next admission
into it, and only the main sessions' copy of its prompt was parked: the
next turn of that conversation read the reply again.

STRATA_SLOT_PARK=1 (default off) captures a slot's conversation when it
ends (BDONE): its tokens, the running state at its end and its K/V, on
one persistent thread per stage device through pinned staging blocks of
its own, while the other slots decode, without a device-wide wait (the
slot's last window has left every stage).  A group whose pad row would
write a slot still being captured starts after the other groups.  The
image goes to the conversation cache when the slot is overwritten (an
admission into it) or at the next request after a pad row wrote it, and
only then takes the slot's checkpoints along (lazy attach: its turn
checkpoint, and copies of the chain its prompt was read with, made beside
the slots after the admission).  While the slot still holds it the slot
stays the source; a request that continues from the slot drops the image
and takes the chain back.  The main sessions' copy of the admission's
prompt is no longer parked: the slot's image holds it and the reply.  A
slot image has no draft-layer K/V (pipelined slots draft nothing) and is
restored without it, as after a slot's give-back: drafts may differ,
tokens never.  The elastic K/V and runs without --batch-groups keep the
old path.  Retained K/V pages are dropped before a slot's give-back with
the switch too (critique A1).

STRATA_SUPERSEDE_PREFIX=1 (implied by the above; critique A2) decides
which parked copies an outgoing conversation supersedes by tokens: an
entry is dropped when its live tokens start the outgoing ones, or its
deepest checkpoint does and is deeper than the outgoing chain's
shallowest.  With STRATA_SLOT_CKPT_MOVE the chain rule dropped every
conversation that only shared the system prompt's root.

A turn checkpoint parked with a slot's image is marked (slot_turn, run
time only), so the next slot image of that conversation does not carry
the older turns' checkpoints along.

The all-idle timing line is followed by how many group starts waited for
a slot's capture and for how long (24 users x 4 turns: 62 waits, 0.8 s
of one group's time in a 156 s run).

STRATA_SLOT_PARK_VERIFY=1 compares every slot capture with a plain one
before anything writes the slot (ERR on a difference).
STRATA_SLOT_PARK_TEST_RESTORE=1 (tests) puts every idle slot's image into
the cache at the next request, so later turns come back from there.

Tests: batch_test16 (greedy and T=0.7 seed 1234), batch_interleave_test
and batch_overlap_test with VERIFY on: identical to the reference dumps;
batch_interleave_test and batch_groups_cache_test with TEST_RESTORE (the
later turns restored from slot images instead of the slots' give-back):
identical tokens.  Unit: prefix rule, slot_turn copy/compare.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
